WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.343
Teacher midterm practice for C plus plus, question 6.

2
00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.702
What does the last statement, cout A of i, print?

3
00:00:09.402 --> 00:00:14.941
Follow the loop to its end. After i equals three, i plus plus makes i four.

4
00:00:14.941 --> 00:00:19.884
The test i less than four fails, so the loop exits with i equal to four.

5
00:00:20.504 --> 00:00:22.786
Now line thirteen prints A of four.

6
00:00:22.786 --> 00:00:27.785
But A has four elements, indices zero to three. A of four is past the end.

7
00:00:29.385 --> 00:00:32.054
C plus plus does not check array bounds.

8
00:00:32.054 --> 00:00:35.744
Reading past the end compiles fine, and at run time it prints

9
00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:39.492
whatever happens to be in that memory: a garbage value.

10
00:00:39.492 --> 00:00:43.012
On the exam, the teacher writes G, for garbage.

11
00:00:44.613 --> 00:00:48.912
So it prints a garbage value, because i is four, past the end of the array.

12
00:00:49.732 --> 00:00:52.471
Forgetting that the loop variable keeps its final value

13
00:00:52.471 --> 00:00:55.360
after the loop: the value that failed the test.

14
00:00:56.080 --> 00:01:00.953
Exam tip: when a print uses the loop variable after the loop, first write down the

15
00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:05.556
value that made the condition false, then check it against the array size.
